# Keeps `docker build`'s context (everything the Dockerfile's `COPY . .` can see) from
# dragging in this machine's local node_modules, build caches, and .env files — without
# this, a local build from this repo root would ship a possibly Windows-built
# node_modules into the image, which is both wasteful (large, slow to hand to Docker)
# and gets clobbered right after anyway by the Dockerfile's own
# `COPY --from=deps /repo/node_modules ./node_modules` (the deps stage installs a real
# Linux-container node_modules instead). Mirrors .gitignore's own list.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/node_modules/**
.git
.turbo
.next
dist
build
*.tsbuildinfo
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.DS_Store
.vercel
